  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Settles `holder` at the `rate` supplied by the tokenizer and returns their\\ncurrent banked total in SY shares WITHOUT zeroing it. Restricted to the\\ntokenizer. Moves no tokens; it is the first half of a claim.\\n\\nThis is deliberately split from `consume` (they used to be one\\n`settle_and_consume` that zeroed the whole ledger). All-or-nothing consume\\ncould not express a partial payment, but the tokenizer now caps a claim to\\nthe escrow surplus over the senior PT reservation. So it `settle`s to learn\\nthe owed total, decides how much the surplus can cover, and `consume`s only\\nthat. Whatever it does not consume stays banked and is claimable later.\\n\\nThe rate is passed in, not read here, on purpose. The tokenizer is already\\non the call stack when it invokes this (claim_yield -> here), so yt cannot\\ncall back into the tokenizer to fetch the canonical maturity rate: Soroban\\nprohibits re-entering a contract already on the stack. The tokenizer instead\\ncomputes its single canonical rate (live before maturity, its frozen\\nsnapsh",
      "name": "settle",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "holder",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "rate",
          "type_": "i128"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "i128",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
